Subject: Cantor Runtime, Process Procedure, and FPGA Data Design

Description: Formal logical records, keys, relations, lifecycles, cardinalities, retention, sensitivity, migration, and requirement support for the deterministic runtime, process-procedure experiment, and FPGA lowering profile.

@ [data_design_uuid] 6c2f0c0d-2651-4c8b-89dc-cc749ae4adf8
@ [semantic_refinement] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Cantor_Runtime_Procedure_FPGA_Semantic_Refinement_2026-08-05.sop
@ [runtime_exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Deterministic_Runtime_Activation.exploded.sop
@ [procedure_exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Process_Procedure_Experiment.exploded.sop
@ [FPGA_exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_FPGA_Lowering_Profile.exploded.sop

& [IdentityPolicy] is immutable and versioned
  + UUID identifies semantic entity continuity
  + digest identifies exact normalized content
  + generation identifies ordered immutable state revision
  + profile and schema version identify interpretation contract
  + human name and alias are projections only
  + every reference declares expected identity kind and exact or compatible-version policy

& [DeterministicRuntimeRoot] is one supplied state value
  + [key] runtime_state_digest
  + [fields] profile_version, policy_set, logical_clock, repository, calendar, planner_state, lane_state, compiler_fixture_state, bounds, trace_frontier
  + [cardinality] one root contains exactly one logical clock and repository, zero or one calendar and planner projection, zero or more lane sessions, and zero or more bounded compiler fixtures
  + [ownership] caller or test harness owns the value; transition functions return successors
  + [prohibited] ambient singleton, hidden cache authority, external handle, mutable global, system-clock token

& [RuntimeOperation] is a closed tagged union
  + [key] operation_uuid plus expected_runtime_state_digest
  + [variants] append_repository, rebuild_index, advance_logical_time, revise_calendar, expand_recurrence, evaluate_wake, plan, transition_capsule, append_lane_message, join, evaluate_barrier, apply_logical_timeout, run_compiler_forward_fixture, run_compiler_rear_fixture, replay
  + [fields] operation version, caller identity, exact inputs, declared bounds, expected predecessor identities
  + [result] RuntimeReceipt or RuntimeFault and optional successor DeterministicRuntimeRoot

& [RuntimeReceipt] proves one evaluated operation
  + [key] receipt_uuid and normalized digest
  + [fields] operation identity, before digest, after digest when accepted, logical time before and after, emitted identities, trace segment, consumed bounds, disposition
  + [disposition] accepted, refused, faulted, or no_change
  + accepted receipts cannot omit their successor digest

& [RuntimeFault] is typed and non-panicking
  + [categories] invalid_form, unsupported_version, stale_predecessor, missing_reference, duplicate_identity, cycle, bound_exceeded, recurrence_horizon, wake_mismatch, illegal_transition, missing_return, wrong_generation, incomplete_diff, correspondence_missing, forbidden_effect, nondeterminism, internal_invariant
  + [fields] fault UUID, category, operation, subject identities, expected, observed, evidence, safe residual, trace location
  + internal invariant faults preserve diagnostic evidence without claiming recovery

& [RepositoryRuntimeProjection] implements existing pure forms
  + [root] FakeRepositoryState
  + [maps] generations by generation UUID, events by event UUID, content by digest, snapshots by snapshot UUID, indexes by index generation UUID, branch heads by stable branch identity
  + [ordering] admitted event frontier and stable identity order
  + [relation] each accepted RepositoryGeneration has zero or one predecessor within a branch and zero or more declared merge predecessors
  + [rule] derived index entries refer only to identities in their declared source generation

& [CalendarRuntimeProjection] separates temporal roles
  + [root] FakeCalendarState
  + [maps] CalendarItem revisions by stable item UUID and revision, WakeConditions by UUID, commitments by UUID, recurrence expansions by policy digest and horizon
  + [relation] one item has one or more immutable revisions; one revision has zero or more occurrences; one wake cites exactly one version set
  + [rule] provider state enum in the first profile is none or simulated and contains no provider token

& [PlannerRuntimeProjection] is derived and replaceable
  + [root] DeterministicPlannerState
  + [fields] planner profile, selection policy, last admitted PlanRevision identities, optional diagnostic history
  + [input] TaskContract, predecessor plan, repository generation, calendar view, policies, bounds
  + [output] PlanCandidateSet with one or more alternatives or typed refusal
  + [relation] every selected edge cites its dependency evidence and stable tie-break

& [TandemRuntimeProjection] binds exact cursors
  + [root] LaneSessionState keyed by session UUID and generation
  + [children] participant set, LaneCursors, LaneMessages, ReflectionReturns, ObserverJoin candidates, ReleaseBarriers, logical timeout policies, residuals
  + [relation] every message belongs to exactly one session generation and cites zero or more causal predecessors from the same or an explicitly bridged generation
  + [rule] join and barrier receipts refer to the exact required identity set and cannot use counts alone

& [CompilerFixtureProjection] is bounded data
  + [root] CompilerFixtureState keyed by fixture UUID and generation
  + [children] source objects, SemanticIR objects, BuildIR objects, target metadata, CompilerImpact, DiffRecords, correspondence evidence, proof expectations, diagnostics
  + [relation] a checked rear result cites an independently generated correspondence evidence identity
  + [rule] downstream invalidation contains exact affected nodes and preserved unrelated nodes

& [ProcedureCandidateRecord] preserves authored intent
  + [key] candidate_uuid and source_digest
  + [fields] author, provenance, purpose, scope, language profile, source text or normalized source form, SOP anchor set, input and output schemas, process declarations, effects, bounds, created logical time
  + [sensitivity] inherits the highest input source and declared anchor sensitivity
  + [status] candidate only

& [ProcedureSchemaSet] is closed and versioned
  + [key] schema_set_digest
  + [members] input, output, message, event, process-local state, procedure state, invocation result, fault
  + [bounds] each collection and text-bearing field declares maximum size
  + [compatibility] exact by default; explicit migration required for any non-exact invocation

& [ProcessDefinition] is static compiled meaning
  + [key] process_definition_uuid within procedure identity
  + [fields] name, role identity, initial state, accepted message tags, emitted message tags, transition regions, terminal states, resource contribution
  + [cardinality] one procedure has one or more process definitions in the experiment
  + [rule] process names are unique within one canonical procedure

& [CantorProcessIRRecord] is the portable waist
  + [key] IR_digest
  + [fields] IR version, source digest, type table, schema set, constant table, SOP anchor table, process definitions, control regions, effect table, bound table, source map, normalized encoding
  + [rule] no backend-specific address, pointer, clock, register, ABI padding, instruction opcode, or vendor identity changes semantic digest

& [ProcessInstanceState] is an immutable continuation
  + [key] invocation_uuid plus process_instance_uuid plus generation
  + [fields] definition ref, program region and point, local state, inbox frontier, outbox frontier, awaited condition, lifecycle, logical time, remaining budgets
  + [lifecycle] ready, operating, yielded, waiting, passivated, terminal_return, terminal_fault, cancelled
  + [transition] one ProcessStep consumes one exact generation and returns at most one successor generation

& [NegotiationSession] models shared inference explicitly
  + [key] session_uuid and frame_generation
  + [fields] purpose, required participants, optional observers, pinned SOP anchor set, policy, NegotiatedFrame, token holder, pass set, message frontier, status
  + [status] opened, deliberating, stable_candidate, admitted, refused, timed_out, cancelled, faulted
  + [relation] each generation has exactly one frame and zero or more messages; stable_candidate requires pass set equality with required participants

& [ProcedurePhaseReceipts] keep authority disjoint
  + [records] ValidationReceipt, CompilationReceipt, VerificationReceipt, AdmissionDisposition, CatalogueReceipt, RevocationRecord
  + [key] receipt UUID and subject exact identity
  + [rule] each receipt states only its own phase and cannot imply a later phase
  + [cardinality] one compiled procedure has exactly one source and compiler identity, one or more verification attempts, zero or one active admission, and zero or more revocation or supersession records

& [ProcedureCatalogueState] is an in-memory projection in the first experiment
  + [key] catalogue generation digest
  + [maps] admitted procedure exact identity to status, alias and version to exact identities, revocation by procedure identity
  + [rule] catalogue records cite AdmissionDisposition and never embed a capability not named by admission

& [InvocationRequestAndResult] close the tool transaction
  + [request_key] invocation_uuid
  + [request_fields] caller, purpose, admitted procedure, schemas, input, SOP generation, policy, participants, logical time, step and memory budgets, expected result schema
  + [result_fields] invocation UUID, procedure exact identity, disposition, typed output or fault, final process states, normalized semantic trace, consumed budgets, residuals, proof refs
  + [cardinality] one accepted request yields exactly one terminal result in the deterministic harness

& [SemanticTrace] is backend-independent evidence
  + [key] trace_digest
  + [events] invocation_started, process_selected, state_replaced, message_emitted, message_received, yielded, waiting, reactivated, joined, frame_revised, participant_passed, returned, faulted, budget_refused, invocation_completed
  + [fields] logical index, process and procedure identity, subject generation, normalized payload digest, causal predecessors
  + [exclusion] physical cycle count and transport timing belong to backend telemetry, not semantic trace

& [FPGATargetProfileRecord] is non-executable now
  + [key] profile UUID and version
  + [fields] eligible IR subset, prohibited operations, bounds, interface schema, scheduling semantics, correspondence rules, evidence requirements, authority grade
  + [absent] device, board, vendor, toolchain, clock, memory map, bitstream, driver, credential, loading authority

& [FutureHardwareCandidateRecords] are schema guidance only
  + [records] KernelProfileEvidence, TargetIdentity, ToolchainIdentity, InterfaceContract, SynthesisEvidence, TimingEvidence, ResourceEvidence, HardwareCorrespondenceReceipt, BitstreamIdentity, DeviceAdmissionDisposition
  + [rule] their declaration in data design creates no present instance or implementation authority

& [RetentionAndSensitivity] preserve audit without overcollection
  + raw procedure source, SOP anchor refs, admissions, revocations, and proof-bearing traces retain according to declared policy
  + invocation inputs and outputs inherit sensitivity and may be represented by digest plus authorized locator when raw retention is prohibited
  + derived indexes and catalogues may be rebuilt and retired without deleting source admissions
  + failed and superseded candidates retain minimal diagnostic lineage sufficient for audit and recurrence prevention
  + secret material, provider credentials, hardware keys, and private chain-of-thought are prohibited data classes in the first profiles

& [MigrationBoundary] is explicit
  + profile, schema, IR, compiler, verifier, policy, SOP anchor, and backend revisions are independent version axes
  + migration is a separately identified deterministic transform with before, after, diagnostics, loss, and proof
  + no compatibility is inferred from matching names or similar structure
  + first implementations may support exact version only and fail closed otherwise

& [RequirementSupportSummary] is complete at data-design grade
  + CDRA-001 through CDRA-040 map to runtime root, operation, receipt, fault, repository, calendar, planner, tandem, compiler, trace, bounds, and migration records
  + CPPE-001 through CPPE-040 map to candidate, schemas, process definition, IR, instance, session, phase receipts, catalogue, invocation, trace, bounds, and effect rules
  + CFLP-001 through CFLP-024 map to target profile, future candidate records, semantic trace, correspondence, and absent-authority fields
  + physical persistence, service concurrency, model provider, syntax aesthetics, backend encoding, HDL, HLS, target, and device remain unselected

& [DataDesignDisposition] is stable_for_constraints_and_justification
  + identities, keys, relations, cardinalities, lifecycle, sensitivity, retention, effects, migration, and cross-profile seams are explicit
  + implementation evidence remains none
